- [ ] Run BOLA test (F-01, F-02) with User A's token on User B's object IDs
- [ ] Decode JWT and check expiry (F-03)
- [ ] Test token reuse after logout (F-03)
- [ ] Compare API response fields with UI fields (F-04)
- [ ] Run Collection Runner with 100 login attempts (F-05)
- [ ] Send extra fields in update request (F-06)
- [ ] Send malformed JSON and wrong HTTP method (F-07)
- [ ] Save screenshots of each request and response as evidence

## Appendix B: Security Terms (Plain Language)

| Term | Simple Meaning |
|------|----------------|
| Authentication | Proving who you are (login) |
| Authorization | Checking what you are allowed to access |
| Token | A digital pass that proves you are logged in |
| Rate limiting | Restricting how many requests one user can make in a time period |
| Mass assignment | Accidentally letting users change fields they should not control |
